{"crc":"03f44890","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `django/db/backends/base/schema.py` in the `_delete_composed_index` method. When there's both a `unique_together` and an `index_together` on the same fields, deleting the `index_together` fails because it finds two constraints (the unique constraint and the index) instead of just one.\n\nThe fix should make the constraint lookup more specific by looking for the index constraint specifically, not just any constraint on those columns.\n\nLet me search for the relevant method in the file:\n\n```python\ndef _delete_composed_index(self, model, fields, *args):\n```\n\nThis method needs to be modified to properly handle the case where both a unique constraint and an index exist on the same columns. The fix should filter constraints to only find the index constraint, not the unique constraint.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/backends/base/schema.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def _delete_composed_index(self, model, fields, *args):\n        \"\"\"\n        Delete the index on the given model for the given fields.\n        \"\"\"\n        constraint_names = self._constraint_names(model, [f.column for f in fields])\n        if len(constraint_names) != 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Found wrong number (%s) of constraints for %s(%s)\" % (\n                len(constraint_names),\n                model._meta.db_table,\n                \", \".join(f.column for f in fields),\n            ))\n        self.execute(self._delete_constraint_sql(self.sql_delete_index, model, constraint_names[0]))\n=======\n    def _delete_composed_index(self, model, fields, *args):\n        \"\"\"\n        Delete the index on the given model for the given fields.\n        \"\"\"\n        constraint_names = self._constraint_names(model, [f.column for f in fields], index=True)\n        if len(constraint_names) != 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Found wrong number (%s) of constraints for %s(%s)\" % (\n                len(constraint_names),\n                model._meta.db_table,\n                \", \".join(f.column for f in fields),\n            ))\n        self.execute(self._delete_constraint_sql(self.sql_delete_index, model, constraint_names[0]))\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQWF6ESGWWQ1SCAZ6AXCVM7","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQWF6EP3HS7R1RHEZ6XB583"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786434274.025505}
